// The package's phase modules: the adapters a `import syntax` may name.
//
// A module here is not written in the language ordinary source is written in.
// It is checked and evaluated in the expansion phase, where the syntax types
// are in scope, and it is reached only through a syntax import — an ordinary
// `import` cannot change syntax, and an ordinary reader of one of these
// modules would be reading names that ordinary source has no way to spell.

mod doubled;
mod graph;
mod staff;
